Lines: 29

Poor performance on the Computing Center's Sequent cluster (mentor.cc, sage.cc,
and expert.cc) continues to impact instructional usage of these machines. 
There is no single cause for this poor performance other than an increase in
load beyond the capacity of various components.  While we continue to
investigate ways to improve the efficiency of handling this load, it is
also clear that we have to find ways of reducing the peak load.

While activity on these machines is governed by the PUCC policies on
appropriate use (see ZZ-POLICY), it is now necessary to specify a more
specific and restrictive policy during peak periods.  Effective
7:30 am, Monday 2/14, we are asking students to observe the following
usage restrictions on these machines.

	Between 7:30 am and 10 pm, Monday - Friday, only the following usage
	is permitted:

		- Computing directly assigned by a faculty member in
		  support of a class you are currently taking
		- Reading, saving, composing, and sending e-mail
		- Reading, saving, composing, and sending net news items

	At all other times, normal PUCC appropriate use policies apply.

Specifically, during the prime time periods, or whenever it would interfere
with work directly assigned by a class, "personal computing", other than
e-mail and net news, is not permitted.  Faculty members and research staff
with accounts on these machines are also asked to observe these restrictions,
when possible.

